Recursion :  A Function Called By itslef until a specific Conditions Meet .
Example :
f(){
 print(1)
 f();
  }
main(){
   f();
  }

This Function called by itslef and goes on ..because it does not have an exit condition .It is called Infinite Recursion . it runs out of memory => stack overflow .
In stack  f(1) => f(2) => f(3) => f(4) ... not been completed it is waiting in stack . segmentation error .

Base condition => condition to stop a recursion call .
